Package: cape-core
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 python3.12,
 python3-poetry,
 postgresql,
 postgresql-client,
 clamav,
 clamav-daemon,
 clamav-freshclam,
 suricata | cape-suricata,
 yara,
 qemu-kvm | cape-qemu,
 qemu-utils | cape-qemu,
 ovmf,
 libvirt-clients,
 libvirt-daemon-system,
 virtinst,
 bridge-utils,
 unzip,
 jq,
 curl,
 git,
 cron,
 numactl
Description: CAPEv2 sandbox application core
 The Python application code for the CAPEv2 fork plus our patches as commits.
 Bundled venv via dh-virtualenv at /opt/CAPEv2/.venv/, configs under
 /etc/cape/ via dpkg conffile mechanism, systemd units in
 /lib/systemd/system/. Replaces the legacy git-clone + pip-install +
 patch-apply bootstrap path.

Package: cape-signatures
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 cape-core (>= ${binary:Version})
Description: CAPEv2 community signatures and parsers
 Python content from the kevoreilly/community repo: behavioral signatures
 (modules/signatures/) and malware-family config parsers (modules/parsers/).
 Version-pinned to cape-core via apt Depends so signature/core ABI mismatch
 is caught at install time rather than at runtime via ImportError.

# cape-qemu and cape-suricata are NOT built from this source package any
# more. They're produced by dedicated workflows (qemu-build.yml and
# suricata-build.yml) so cape-core and cape-signatures rebuild fast on
# every push instead of paying the 25-min QEMU compile each time. The
# .deb files apt-publish ships still satisfy cape-core's `... |
# cape-{qemu,suricata}` alternation in the Depends: above.
#
# Build inputs that live in this repo and feed into those workflows:
#   suricata-build/build.sh + package.sh       → cape-suricata.deb
#   qemu-build/<tbd>                           → cape-qemu.deb
#   debian/cape-suricata.{install,postinst}    → file-list manifest +
#   debian/cape-qemu.{install,postinst}          deb postinst respectively;
#                                                consumed by package.sh
#                                                in each *-build/ dir.
